292
00:10:26,284 --> 00:10:28,784
So what killed Quibi?

293
00:10:28,784 --> 00:10:30,234
Not one thing.

294
00:10:30,234 --> 00:10:31,362
The pandemic,

295
00:10:31,362 --> 00:10:32,951
a phone-only design,

296
00:10:32,951 --> 00:10:35,024
and shows nobody felt they had to

297
00:10:35,024 --> 00:10:35,854
see.

298
00:10:35,994 --> 00:10:38,534
But underneath was a bigger mistake.

299
00:10:38,534 --> 00:10:40,756
Quibi raised the money first and found

300
00:10:40,756 --> 00:10:43,134
out what people wanted later.

301
00:10:43,154 --> 00:10:44,906
It bet that money could buy an

302
00:10:44,906 --> 00:10:45,884
audience.

303
00:10:45,884 --> 00:10:46,926
In streaming,

304
00:10:46,926 --> 00:10:48,454
money buys shows.

305
00:10:48,454 --> 00:10:50,664
Only habits buy viewers.

306
00:10:50,694 --> 00:10:53,034
And short videos on phones did become

307
00:10:53,034 --> 00:10:54,804
a huge business.

308
00:10:54,834 --> 00:10:56,984
Just not one that people paid a

309
00:10:56,984 --> 00:10:58,659
subscription for.

310
00:10:58,917 --> 00:11:01,343
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

311
00:11:01,343 --> 00:11:04,236
we follow the money behind another hidden

312
00:11:04,236 --> 00:11:06,617
link of the world economy.

313
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:09,321
This is The Hidden Economics.
